# NSG Phase 2a — RU sleep states (deep / light / micro) on the real ns-O-RAN engine.
#
# Applies to the ns-3.42 mmWave fork in the Ubuntu-2004-nsoran distro
# (/home/builder/ns-O-RAN-flexric/mmwave-LENA-oran). Four pieces:
#
#  1. mmwave-radio-energy-model-enb.{h,cc} — the model already DECLARED
#     m_lightSleepCurrentA / m_microSleepCurrentA and never used them (a cell was
#     either serving or 0 A "off"). They become real attributes SleepMicroA /
#     SleepLightA / SleepDeepA with state codes 5/6/7, per-state time accounting
#     and GetStateTime(), which adds the in-progress slice — the counters are
#     only credited on LEAVING a state, so a parked radio read 0 for it.
#     Defaults follow the flexible BS power model (Debaillie et al., VTC 2015):
#     micro ~0.69, light ~0.50, deep ~0.33 of the active-idle draw.
#
#  2. mmwave-spectrum-phy.cc — ChangeState hardcoded m_intState=4 (0 A) whenever
#     TX power was 0. It now asks the device for its sleep-state code, so a
#     sleeping cell is charged its depth's current instead of nothing.
#
#  3. mmwave-enb-net-device.h — that per-device code (Set/GetSleepStateCode).
#
#  4. scenario-zero-with_parallel_loging.cc — the controller itself:
#     gnbSleepFile ('depth,idle_ms,wake_ms' per gNB), sleepWakeLoadPct,
#     sleepIdleDutyPct, sleepWakeHoldMs, sleepTickMs; a periodic tick that
#     descends idle cells after their shutdown timer, wakes them on serving-cell
#     load after a REAL wake-up delay (the cell is off the air meanwhile), keeps
#     a coverage floor, and logs [NSG-SLEEP] transitions + [NSG-SLEEP-SUM] duty
#     summaries. Also: the periodic energy print now reads the model's LIVE
#     total — the trace only fires on a state CHANGE, so a parked cell's draw
#     silently vanished from the totals.
#
# Rebuild: runuser -u builder -- bash -lc "cd $NS3DIR && ./ns3 build"
#          then engines/nsoran/build-slim.sh and restart nsg-engine.
